### Docker Port Mapping ###
docker pull jenkins
docker run -it --name jenkins_host -p 8081:8080 jenkins
xx.xx.xx.xx:8081 (To access the page in browser)

### Detached Mode ###
docker pull jenkins
docker -d --name jenkins_host -p 8082:8080 jenkins
docker ps
@ You will exit out from container and see the container list

### Attach Mode ###
docker attach xxxxxxx (container_ID) Will attach the terminal to the same process.

### exec Mode ###
docker exec -it xxxxxxx (container_ID) Will open a new session without disturbing the old process.

### Docker Volumes ###
Volumes 
*Volumes are recommended beacuse it was managed by docker itself*

docker volume ls
docker volume create db_data01
docker volume ls
cd /var/lib/docker/volumes (To see all the created volumes)
docker run -d --name cont1 -p 8083:8080 -v db_data01:/app/data jenkins (If container deleted you can find the stored data in /var/lib/docker/volumes/db_data01/_data)
docker volume inspect db_data01
docker volume rm db_data01

Bind mounts
*mount points created with in the host system*

docker run -d -v HM:RM db_data02
docker run -d -v /opt/logs:/opt/logs db_data02

### Tpes of docker networks ###

1. bridge   -> Default local container communication
2. host     -> Share host network
3. none     -> No networking
4. overlay  -> Multi-Docker host communication
5. macvlan  -> Container gets real LAN IP

docker network ls
docker network inspect bridge

* Create Custom Network *
docker network create stag_network
docker network ls
docker network inspect stag_network
docker run -d --name stag_cont -p 8081:8080 -v db_data01:/var/lib/msql -n stag_network jenkins

docker tag 
docker push awscloudfordevops/practice_images:jenkins

